        {# ── Install teaching ── #}
        <section class="shelf-section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-heading">
            <h2 id="install-heading" class="shelf-h2">Where <code>ionrift-data</code> lives</h2>
            <p class="shelf-note">
                Foundry’s <strong>Data</strong> folder is the root. Create <code>ionrift-data</code> next to <code>modules</code> and <code>worlds</code> if it is not there yet.
                Unzip so each pack’s <code>overlay-manifest.json</code> sits in its subfolder, then reload the world.
            </p>

            <div class="shelf-fs-grid">
                <figure class="shelf-fs-panel">
                    <figcaption>Before</figcaption>
                    <pre class="shelf-fs-tree" aria-label="Data folder before overlays">Data/
├── modules/
├── systems/
├── worlds/
└── (no ionrift-data yet)</pre>
                </figure>
                <figure class="shelf-fs-panel shelf-fs-panel--after">
                    <figcaption>After (example)</figcaption>
                    <pre class="shelf-fs-tree" aria-label="Data folder after overlays">Data/
├── modules/
├── systems/
├── worlds/
└── ionrift-data/
    └── overlays/
        ├── ionrift-respite/
        │   ├── core/
        │   │   └── overlay-manifest.json
        │   └── cooking/
        │       └── overlay-manifest.json
        └── ionrift-quartermaster/
            └── core/
                └── overlay-manifest.json</pre>
                </figure>
            </div>

            <ul class="shelf-host-notes">
                <li><strong>Self-hosted:</strong> open the Foundry User Data path from Setup, or your host’s file browser for that volume.</li>
                <li><strong>Hosted Foundry:</strong> use the host’s asset / file manager and place the same folder tree under Data.</li>
                <li><strong>Compiled zip:</strong> overlays only. Extract at the Data root so <code>ionrift-data/overlays/...</code> lands in the right place. Module zips are separate.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

